---
layout: room.njk
description: "Love Your Food Plan: AI-powered meal plans built around your dietary approaches, restrictions, and personal preferences. A macOS app with no login and no cloud."
lede: "Meal planning that starts with what you love. AI-powered meal plans built around your dietary approaches, restrictions, and personal preferences."
privacyLine: "Your plans and recipes stay on your Mac. Text goes to Anthropic, with your own API key, only when you ask the app to generate something."
distribution: "Direct download, signed and notarized; updates itself"
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import plaque -%}
{%- set a = apps | app(appSlug) -%}
<section class="exhibits menu" aria-label="In this room">
  <div class="menu-open">
    <h2><b>Love</b> your food plan!</h2>
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="wall-copy">When you want to change your food plan, starting with recipes isn’t helpful. They’re too detailed, you have to sift through a million ingredients to check for restrictions, and recipe websites are notoriously cluttered, difficult to use, and filled with ads.</p>
      <p class="wall-copy soft">Instead, <b>start with what you like and what you need to avoid,</b> and use AI to generate meal plans for you. Maybe you want to make leftovers, maybe you need some child-friendly options. When you see meals you like, you can generate recipes.</p>
      <p class="wall-copy">If you’ve ever struggled to change your food plan and keep reverting to the same old things you’re already <s>familiar</s> bored with, it’s exciting to see breakfasts, lunches, dinners, and snacks that sound like you’d love them!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol class="courses" aria-label="Four steps to a meal plan">
    <li class="course">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-approaches.webp" alt="The Dietary Approaches window, with chips for approaches such as Anti-Inflammatory, Low-Glycemic, and Mediterranean selected, plus a custom approach, Bright Line Eating." width="1800" height="984" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>Dietary approaches</b>Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="step">Step 1</p>
        <h3>Start with your big-picture dietary approach</h3>
        <p>Just click the ones you want to use. Click the info button to get a description; maybe you’ll want to try a new approach. Add custom approaches, and the AI will figure them out.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="course flip">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-restrictions.webp" alt="The Dietary Restrictions window, with Gluten set to Mild and Histamine set to Moderate among common restrictions including Halal and Kosher." width="1800" height="973" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>Dietary restrictions</b>Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="step">Step 2</p>
        <h3>Set your dietary restrictions</h3>
        <p>Click the ones that apply to you or your family. Set each to Mild, Moderate, or Strict, and the meal selections will match. Custom restrictions welcome.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="course">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-preferences.webp" alt="The food preferences screen: a grid of vegetables, each with buttons from Strong Like to Strong Dislike, beside food groups with summary counts." width="1600" height="1140" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>Food preferences</b>Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="step">Step 3</p>
        <h3>Set your detailed food preferences</h3>
        <p>In five minutes you can design a set of preferences that guarantees you’ll like the meals suggested. Click once for each food, from Strong Like to Strong Dislike.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="course flip">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-new-meal-plan.webp" alt="The New Meal Plan window, with options for cooking complexity, servings, how many of each meal, cuisines, leftovers, child-friendly options, and special instructions." width="1800" height="1278" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>New meal plan</b>Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="step">Step 4</p>
        <h3>Generate a meal plan</h3>
        <p>Set cooking complexity from minimal assembly to elaborate weekend cooking. Choose how many breakfasts, lunches, dinners, and snacks. Add leftovers, child-friendly options, cuisine preferences, or special instructions.</p>
        <p>Click Generate and wait ten seconds.</p>
        <img class="wait" src="/assets/img/foodplan-generating.webp" alt="A progress bar reading Generating your meal plan." width="1182" height="164" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="spread">
    <div class="spread-head">
      <h2>Look at all these awesome meals!</h2>
      <p>If one doesn’t appeal, click New Suggestion and Claude will make another, avoiding ingredients already used in the surrounding meals. Use it as a weekly plan or just a reference for new ideas.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="exhibit">
      <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-meal-plan.webp" alt="A week’s meal plan called Peruvian Bright Weeknights, with breakfast, lunch, and dinner, each offering three meals with their ingredients and buttons for a new suggestion or a recipe." width="1800" height="1172" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption><b>Peruvian Bright Weeknights</b>A generated meal plan. Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="pair">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-carnivore.webp" alt="Carnivore lunches and dinners, including Coconut Aminos Chicken Bowl, Bacon-Wrapped Asparagus with Eggs, and Pan-Seared Lamb Chops with Asparagus." width="1800" height="704" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>Committed carnivore? Covered.</b>A carnivore plan. Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-vegan.webp" alt="Vegan lunches and dinners, including Hummus Veggie Tortilla Wraps, Red Lentil Soup, and Black Bean Corn Skillet Tacos." width="1800" height="734" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>Fully vegan? Every meal fits.</b>A vegan plan. Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="between">And everything in between.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="course flip">
    <figure class="exhibit">
      <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-recipe.webp" alt="A recipe for Peruvian lemongrass chicken thighs with roasted potatoes and kale, with ingredients in two columns, eight numbered steps, and prep and cook times." width="1800" height="1172" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption><b>From a meal to a recipe</b>Recipe view. Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Generate recipes</h3>
      <p>Click Generate Recipe and get a detailed recipe with ingredients, cooking steps, and no clutter. Recipes are editable, so you can tweak them to your taste.</p>
      <p>Prints great too: recipes and meal plans both export to clean PDFs. Click the download icon in the upper right corner.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="course facts">
    <figure class="exhibit">
      <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-nutrition-label.webp" alt="An FDA-style Nutrition Facts label for the lemongrass chicken recipe, with per-serving and per-recipe columns for calories, macronutrients, vitamin D, calcium, iron, and potassium." width="1094" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption><b>Nutrition Facts</b>Estimated for one recipe. Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Nutrition labels for every recipe</h3>
      <p>Click Estimate Nutrition on any recipe and get a complete FDA-style Nutrition Facts label: calories, fat, protein, carbs, fiber, sodium, vitamins, and minerals, per serving and per recipe.</p>
      <p>Values are estimated from USDA FoodData Central, the same database dietitians use. It’s not a substitute for medical advice, but it’s a solid way to understand what you’re actually eating, and to make better choices without guessing.</p>
      <p>Great for tracking macros, watching sodium, comparing recipes side by side, or just being more intentional about what goes on your plate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="course flip">
    <figure class="exhibit">
      <img src="/assets/img/foodplan-api-key.webp" alt="The Set Up Your AI Provider panel, with four steps: create an Anthropic account, add credits, create an API key, and paste it into the app." width="1600" height="773" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption><b>Set up your AI provider</b>Screen capture from the app.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Get your own AI for food plans</h3>
      <p>You’ll connect the app to Claude, the AI. It’s simple, and the app steps you through it: you create an account with Anthropic, the company behind Claude, and buy a minimum of $5 in credits. No subscription, and credits last for a year.</p>
      <p>The app tracks the costs for you. A typical meal plan costs a few cents, and a recipe usually a penny or two, so $5 goes a long way. You pay Anthropic directly; Individuate never sees your data or takes a cut.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="menu-close">
    <h2>Download for Mac</h2>
    <p>For Mac laptops and desktops, not iPhone or iPad. Old-school macOS app. No login. No cloud. Completely free, with no demo mode and no ads.</p>
    {% if a.download %}
    <div class="actions">
      {{ plaque(a) }}
      <span class="note">{% for r in a.requires %}{{ r[0] }} {{ r[1] }}{% endfor %} · {{ a.note or "No account needed" }}</span>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
